  </div></div>

  <!-- ====== ABOUT ====== -->
  <section id="about"><div class="wrap split rev">
    <div>
      <p class="tag">/ ABOUT THE EVENT</p>
      <h2>Where <span class="grad">code</span> meets creativity.</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--mut)">WEB-A-THON has grown into the most awaited technical showdown of NIRVAN. In its 4th edition, participants get a live problem statement, a fixed clock, and complete creative freedom — from wireframe to working deployment.</p>
      <p style="color:var(--mut);margin-top:14px">Whether you are a first-year student writing your first media query or a final-year full-stack developer, WEB-A-THON 4.0 is built to push your limits, sharpen your teamwork, and put your work in front of expert judges from academia and industry.</p>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">Open to all branches</span><span class="chip">Beginner friendly</span>
        <span class="chip">Mentor support</span><span class="chip">Certificates for all</span>
        <span class="chip">Live judging</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shot"><img src="pic7.jpeg" alt="Students coding at Web-a-thon"><span class="cap">// TECH GEEKS CLUB · GEHU HALDWANI</span></div>
  </div></section>

  <!-- ====== TRACKS ====== -->
  <section id="tracks"><div class="wrap rev">
    <div class="head"><p class="tag">/ PROBLEM TRACKS</p>
      <h2>Pick your <span class="grad">battlefield</span></h2>
      <p>Choose one track at the time of registration. The exact problem statement inside your track is revealed at the opening ceremony.</p></div>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">🎨</div><h3>UI / UX Design</h3><p>Craft high-fidelity, accessible interfaces in Figma or code. Judged on visual hierarchy, usability and originality.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">🌐</div><h3>Frontend Development</h3><p>Pure HTML, CSS and JavaScript or a framework of your choice. Responsiveness and performance carry weight.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">⚙️</div><h3>Full-Stack Web App</h3><p>Ship a working product with authentication, database and a deployed link. Bonus points for clean architecture.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">🤖</div><h3>AI-Powered Web</h3><p>Integrate an API or model into a meaningful web experience that solves a real campus or community problem.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">🏔️</div><h3>Web for Uttarakhand</h3><p>Build for local impact — tourism, agriculture, disaster alerts, hill education or Himalayan heritage.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico">🚀</div><h3>Open Innovation</h3><p>Got an idea that fits nowhere else? Pitch it. Surprise the judges with something nobody expected.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <!-- ====== SCHEDULE ====== -->
  <section id="schedule"><div class="wrap split rev" style="align-items:start">
    <div>
      <div class="head"><p class="tag">/ SCHEDULE</p><h2>Event <span class="grad">timeline</span></h2>
        <p>Two days of ideation, building and pitching at the Haldwani Campus auditorium and computer labs.</p></div>
      <div class="tl">
        <div class="ev"><span>DAY 01 · 09:00 AM</span><h4>Registration &amp; Check-in</h4><p>Team verification, ID cards and lab allotment.</p></div>
        <div class="ev"><span>DAY 01 · 10:30 AM</span><h4>Inauguration &amp; Problem Reveal</h4><p>Address by the faculty coordinators and release of track-wise problem statements.</p></div>
        <div class="ev"><span>DAY 01 · 11:00 AM</span><h4>Coding Begins ⏱️</h4><p>The 24-hour clock starts. Mentors rotate through the labs.</p></div>
        <div class="ev"><span>DAY 01 · 06:00 PM</span><h4>Mentor Review — Round 1</h4><p>Progress checkpoint and feedback on design direction.</p></div>
        <div class="ev"><span>DAY 02 · 11:00 AM</span><h4>Code Freeze &amp; Submission</h4><p>Push to GitHub and submit your deployed link.</p></div>
